print("DEMO: LEFTS-inspired composable experiment acceptance");
print("Scenario: consolidate what five runnable teaching demos prove, what their adversarial gates reject, and which abstractions should or should not be promoted.");
print("Native boundary: all substantive Split, grouped fitting, Ensemble, Feed, Tune, metrics, parity, and IR work is MLPL. The runtime supplies only generic callable, record, array, Result, JSON, and numeric facilities.");
print("Budgets: every component enforces its own row, group, candidate, identity-comparison, magnitude, graph-node, graph-edge, decode-element, and output-byte ceilings; acceptance reruns every component twice and requires byte-identical stdout.");
print("Concept evidence:"); print({Split:"disjoint visible train/validation/evaluation identities",Lift:"one fitted parameter per group without special syntax",Ensemble:"visible disagreement and deterministic ordered mean",Feed:"visible upstream feature and harmful no-feed ablation",Tune:"all validation scores, deterministic tie rule, and one held-out evaluation"});
print("Outcome highlights:"); print({grouped_learning:"global MSE 9 -> grouped MSE 0",ensemble:"member MSE 1/1 -> aggregate MSE 0",feed:"fed MSE 0 versus ablation MSE 32.6667",tune:"offset scores 1/0/1; selected offset 1; held-out MSE 0",rolling:"two refits, exact explicit parity, seven-node/six-edge validated IR"});
print("Promotion decisions:"); print({callable_records:"retain as the reusable MLPL computation-interface pattern",grouped_fit:"retain as a concrete local MLPL helper",ensemble_feed_tune:"retain as teaching combinators until another consumer proves a generic API",computation_ir:"candidate for broader extraction only after a non-ML consumer",generic_functor:"do not add; current law evidence is container-specific",sw_mlpl:"no change justified",native_extension:"no capability gap found",new_repository:"not justified"});
print("Limitations:"); print({scope:"tiny deterministic scalar learners",compatibility:"inspired by LEFTS; not Python API compatible",execution:"sequential and in-memory",formal_category:"no category, morphism mapping, or general functor protocol is defined",production:"no claim of distributed tuning, GPU training, caching, or production optimization"});
print("ACCEPTANCE concepts=Split,Lift,Ensemble,Feed,Tune"); print("ACCEPTANCE deterministic_reruns=yes"); print("PROMOTION sw_mlpl_changes=none"); print("PROMOTION native_extensions=none"); print("CLAIM formal_functor_protocol=no");
print("Interpretation: sw-MLPL already expresses the useful LEFTS-inspired composition story as ordinary inspectable library code. The strongest reusable result is the callable-record computation interface plus explicit dataflow; adding keywords, Rust semantics, a generic Functor protocol, or a new repository would currently add machinery without demonstrated need."); ok(1)
